  "worked_solution": "The Law of Sines states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡A}{a}=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡B}{b}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have\n\n$$\na=20,\\,m∠B={35}^{∘},\\,b=12,\n$$\n\nand therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡A}{20} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡{35}^{∘}}{12} \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡A & =20\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡{35}^{∘}}{12} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{35}^{∘}}{3} \\\\  & ≈\\frac{5\\cdot 0.574}{3} \\\\  & ≈0.957,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to five decimal places.\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠A & ≈\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(0.957)≈{73}^{∘},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest degree.",
